.\" dcheck(1) — device health check
.TH DCHECK 1 "2026" "dcheck" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dcheck \- inspect storage (SSD/HDD/NVMe) identity, health and remaining life
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dcheck
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dcheck
reads whole-disk block devices and reports identity, capacity, interface link
speed and SMART health (verdict, temperature, power-on hours, TBW, wear, and an
estimated remaining life for 24/7 and 8h/day use).
.PP
It works natively (ATA via
.BR HDIO_DRIVE_CMD ,
NVMe via ioctl, SCSI best-effort) and enriches with
.B smartctl \-a \-j
when smartmontools is installed. It never writes to disks by default.
.PP
Device data is read from
.I /sys/block
so disks are listed as soon as they are attached, mounted or not.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B (none)
Interactive terminal UI (menu, storage list, scrollable report).
.TP
.BR storage " [" device "] [" \-\-json "] [" \-\-bench "] [" \-\-test " short|long]"
List devices, or report on one. Options:
.BR \-\-json " (machine readable),"
.BR \-\-bench " (read-only sequential + 4K benchmark),"
.BR \-\-test " (start a SMART self-test)."
.TP
.BR check " [" \-\-json ]
One-shot health gate. Exit code reflects the worst verdict.
.TP
.BR watch " [" \-\-interval " S] [" \-\-json "] [" \-\-quiet "] [" \-\-webhook " URL]"
Poll and alert when a device worsens or a new issue appears.
.TP
.BR ram " [" \-\-json ]
Memory report: total/used/available, swap, ECC errors (Linux EDAC), and DIMM
modules (vendor/type/speed/slots) via SMBIOS when
.B dmidecode
is available.
.TP
.BR cpu " [" \-\-json ]
CPU report: model, topology, clock, temperature (Linux), 1-minute load.
.TP
.BR prometheus
Print Prometheus metrics.
.TP
.BR update " [" \-\-check "] [" \-\-force "] [" "\-\-url \fIbase\fP" ]
Download the latest release from
.I https://wayang.dalang.io/dcheck
(or
.BR DCHECK_UPDATE_URL ),
verify its SHA-256 checksum and replace the running binary. Needs write access
to the binary's directory (use sudo for /usr/local/bin). Linux x86_64/aarch64.
.TP
.BR snapshot " \fIdir\fP [" \-\-demo "] [" \-\-mask\-serials "] [" "\-\-host \fIname\fP" "] [" "\-\-size \fIWxH\fP" ]
Render every TUI screen to SVG files in
.I dir
from live data (or demo data), for documentation. Serial numbers can be
masked and the host name replaced before publishing.
.TP
.BR tui " [" \-\-light | \-\-dark "] [" \-\-mouse "] [" \-\-plain "] [" \-\-transparent ]
Terminal UI: a sci-fi HUD with a command deck, storage array, per-device
vitals dashboard and memory/processor dashboards. Uses neon truecolor when the
terminal supports it, else the ANSI palette. Default is dark;
.B \-\-transparent
keeps the terminal background.
.B \-\-plain
uses ASCII borders/symbols for fonts without box-drawing glyphs.
.TP
.BR demo ", " \-\-version ", " \-\-help
See above.
.SH KEYS (TUI)
↑/↓ or j/k move; Enter open; Esc/b back; 1/2/3 jump to storage/memory/processor;
PgUp/PgDn page; Home/End or g/G jump; r rescan/refresh; c copy log (OSC52);
? command reference; q quit. Any key skips the start-up splash.
Text is selectable by default; mouse-wheel scrolling is opt-in with
.BR \-\-mouse .
.SH EXIT STATUS
For
.BR check :
0 ok, 1 unknown/needs root, 2 monitor, 3 backup or replace.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DCHECK_SYS_ROOT
Use an alternate filesystem root containing
.I sys/
and
.I proc/
(for tests or offline images).
.TP
.B DCHECK_SMART_JSON
Parse a captured
.B smartctl \-j
file instead of running smartctl.
.TP
.B DCHECK_SMART_ARGS
Force a smartctl device type, e.g.
.BR "\-d megaraid,0" .
.TP
.B DCHECK_NATIVE
Force the native SMART path (skip smartctl).
.TP
.B DCHECK_CONFIG
Path to a JSON config; default
.IR ~/.config/dcheck/config.json .
.TP
.B DCHECK_THEME
Select the accent:
.B light
(blue) or
.BR dark
(cyan, default).
.TP
.B DCHECK_COLOR
.B truecolor
forces the neon 24-bit palette,
.B ansi
the terminal's 16-colour palette,
.B none
no colour. Default: truecolor when
.B COLORTERM
is
.BR truecolor / 24bit ,
else ansi.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colour entirely.
.TP
.B DCHECK_NO_SPLASH
Skip the TUI start-up splash.
.TP
.B DCHECK_PLAIN
Use ASCII borders/symbols in the TUI.
.TP
.B DCHECK_TRANSPARENT
Keep the terminal background instead of a forced dark/light one.
.TP
.B DCHECK_TBW_JSON
Path to a TBW override map; default
.IR ~/.config/dcheck/tbw.json .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/dcheck/config.json
Optional settings:
.RB { "temp_warn_c": \ 60, "watch_interval": \ 60, "theme": \ "dark", "plain": \ false, "transparent": \ false, "splash": \ true, "hdd_design_years": \ 5 }.
.B hdd_design_years
is the assumed HDD design life at 24/7 (drives do not report one); HDD life is
estimated from it together with the drive's rated start-stop and load-unload
cycles.
.TP
.I ~/.config/dcheck/tbw.json
Rated endurance overrides:
.RB { "model substring": \ TBW_in_TB }.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smartctl (8),
.BR lsblk (8)
.SH AUTHOR
WayangOS contributors (https://github.com/mashanz/wayangos)